What is Homomorphic Encryption?
Homomorphic Encryption is a sophisticated cryptographic technique that enables computation on encrypted data without requiring decryption, creating a foundation for secure data processing in untrusted environments. This transformative technology generates encrypted results that, when decrypted, match the outcome of operations performed on the original plaintext, effectively maintaining data confidentiality throughout the computational process. The primary applications of homomorphic encryption span secure cloud computing, privacy-preserving data analytics, and confidential AI model training, particularly in sectors where data sensitivity is paramount.

